{
 "name": "ln2_quench_fuel_column",
 "description": "24x77 fuel column with built-in LN2 quench: a URAN rod in a TTAN/INWR sleeve under a PSTN control rod, a FILT-framed TSNS ladder (1000/1200 C alternating) with WIFI outputs on the left, an LN2 pocket kept full by CLNE(LN2) at -202 C, and a PCLN(LN2) nozzle beside the rod. Tile at step [24,0].",
 "why": "Save 1289009 (Uranium Power Plant v1.0, Auto mode) repeats this column across its core (x=44,68,...): when the TSNS ladder trips, the console sparks the PCLN(LN2) cells and dumps liquid nitrogen onto the rod stack -- a genuine emergency-quench auto-shutdown, unlike water-injection designs. The LN2 pocket (y=265-266) is self-refilling via CLNE(LN2); both LN2 and its CLNE carry the captured -202 C (cryo lesson: LN2 placed warm boils off instantly). Copied pixel-exact; INSL added on empty faces beside WIFI (lint). Remaining lint criticals are the sensor/WIFI faces that must touch conductors and the PUMP cells that sit inside the lattice by design. The PSTN at the foot is the rod drive; its FRME rod continues below y=300 in the source. Sibling module crmc_uran_fuel_can is the lower 19x35 fuel-can portion of this same 1289009 column; this one is the whole 24px pitch incl. the TSNS ladder and LN2 pocket.",
 "source": "save 1289009, x44-67 y224-300; TSNS (47,234) 1200C, (61,234..250) 1000C; WIFI (44,234) ch57, (64,234..250); LN2 (47-48,265-266) K71 + CLNE(LN2) (47,266) K71; PCLN(LN2) (49,282); URAN (52-56,270-298); PSTN (54,300)",
